":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"font"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPerMinute":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLPerMinute","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPerMinute","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlperminute","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPerMinute","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPerMinute","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The per-minute type can be a number, or a text description including numbers. If a font is specified, it"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overrides the font specified for the overall metronome element. This allows separate specification of a music","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font for the beat-unit and a text font for the numeric value, in cases where a single metronome font is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","